-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261108~sparky9~0 (2026-11-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The splash stays inside the desktop's own depth limits (ORDER 472; Daniel, 2026-11-08: "on plymouth - the separation is
    huge", on a laptop panel in red/cyan). Scaling by the eye's width was right (the same rule as Stereo KWin's), but the
    levels were fixed above the desktop's popped limit: the logo 9.08 px, the base 4.54 and a popping electron 8.54 at 1920,
    against 4 px (kwinrc [StereoDepth] PoppedLimit); at 1366 per eye 5 px against 3. Now the base is half the popped
    limit, the logo and the nearest electron the popped limit (2, 4 and 4 px at 1920), and the farthest electron sinks 4,
    inside the sunk limit of 10
  * A level is placed by its whole disparity, rounded to a pixel with the odd pixel to the left eye; each eye rounded its
    half before, which made every disparity even and, at a few hundred pixels per eye, put base and logo on one level
  * tests/depth-limits.py checks the generated script against the desktop's limits at 1280, 1366, 1920, 2560 and 3840

